snippet.description:
This is a true story from 1997. Somehow, one man was able to hold off 100+ police for over ELEVEN HOURS. In Seattle Washington, Tony Allison, a.ka. "Apollo" was carrying a sword on the street, when   an off-duty police officer initiated the encounter. The officer called in backup, quickly summoning SWAT cars, additional police, fire trucks, and ambulances, and they all quickly surrounded Tony and his katana. This has got to be one of the most absurd police encounters of all time, and the tactics used that day were so absurd that it's hard to believe this is a real story.

Special thanks to Ross at Seattle Public Library for helping me get access to the original 1997 reporting. This reporting revealed certain facts that were not available anywhere online—allowing me to verify the story details using official, primary sources. No other online coverage of this story has done this, so this video brings you the most accurate, firsthand account of what REALLY happened. In particular, I confirmed that the Big Mac offer was indeed real, even though there has been much speculation about it being a fake embellishment.


